  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "IMPRODUCT rejects mixed \"i\"/\"j\" suffixes with #VALUE!, empty text with #NUM!, and formats DBL_MIN as \"0\"",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMPRODUCT(inumber1, [inumber2], ...) folds operands by binary64 complex multiplication, treats blank cells as 0 while rejecting empty text \"\" with #NUM!, returns #VALUE! if operands mix \"i\" and \"j\" suffixes, and formats via Excel's 15-digit complex formatter (emitting \"0\" at DBL_MIN and #NUM! at DBL_MAX). All 3,260 full-bank IMPRODUCT rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (jnt_parity_complex row 596) and CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-complex-format-20260929/batches-answers/answers-batch-improduct.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 3,260/3,260 full-bank rows match.",
